{
  "about": "Whether a landing meets the part of a listen's WHERE a module takes (adapter protocol 2.6's `filter`), as the engine's judge decides it. A module that applies the taken part itself and says `takenApplied: true` must decide every case exactly as the engine does, or the host never re-checks what the module dropped. `filter` is the taken expression a module is handed, `fields` the landing's fields, `holds` the engine's answer. `applied` is whether module-kit applies the filter itself (`takenComparisons` reads it); when false, the module leaves it to the host and says no `takenApplied`. Held by the engine's Rust (crates/movement-engine/src/filter.rs tests, through the listen judge) and module-kit's TypeScript (taken.ts, `takenComparisons` and `holds`).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "case": "numeric texts order as numbers",
      "filter": {
        "type": "compare",
        "op": "gt",
        "left": {
          "type": "edge_property",
          "propertyTypeId": "Amount",
          "fieldOnly": true
        },
        "right": {
          "type": "static",
          "value": "20"
        }
      },
      "fields": {
        "Amount": "100"
      },
      "holds": true,
      "applied": true
    },
    {
      "case": "a numeric text orders against a number",
